tre,_Paris_(22119).jpg","sourceSha1":"e68c80f246cf206a6375ea3ebd957d8d4f1df9f7","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"southwest domes and porch, daylight"},{"title":"File:Basilica of the Sacred Heart of Montmartre, Paris (33846).jpg","author":"Aliva Sahoo","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basilica_of_the_Sacred_Heart_of_Montmartre,_Paris_(33846).jpg","sourceSha1":"256df95a66799bcc9ea25f396f82388ae0970262","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"drum openings, daylight"}],"aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["All 44 mapped part plans and total heights are retained; the north campanile and south entrance remain geographically aligned.","Four 46 m satellite domes lack roof:height in OSM; a 13 m dome above the mapped 33 m drums is inferred from reviewed exterior photographs.","Pale roof material, drum openings, mouldings and small crosses are original simplified visual interpretations.","OSM models the front porch with an enclosing 16 m base: the porch is opened below its mapped 9 m lintel using the mapped porch polygon.","Domes are faceted latitude profiles; sculpture, equestrian figures and fine masonry are omitted."],"source":{"url":"/objects/0be6d60663a42d72a28c5684d1819c9edcaa7801130837554d522ad3423fc5e7/source.blend.gz","bytes":168944,"sha256":"0be6d60663a42d72a28c5684d1819c9edcaa7801130837554d522ad3423fc5e7"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/64d884935424bd523ebea46219b4ee52aa97e2ba4f930657de223220f